Package: konstats
Title: Open Course in Statistics for Linguists
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Massimiliano", "Canzi", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "massimiliano.canzi@uni-konstanz.de",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-6124-0321"))
Description: Materials of two open courses in statistics for linguists,
    Statistics and Advanced Statistics, which are also taught at the
    Department of Linguistics, University of Konstanz. Statistics follows
    Winter (2019) <doi:10.4324/9781315165547> from data wrangling to mixed
    models. Advanced Statistics covers generalised additive mixed models,
    random forests, power analysis, factor analysis and cluster analysis.
    lectures() lists the lectures with their data sets and slides,
    get_tutorial() copies the exercise sheets into a project folder, and an
    'R Markdown' template starts the weekly assignments. install_course()
    installs the packages a course uses and check_setup() tests a computer
    for either course. The helper functions written in the slides of
    Advanced Statistics are included: residual autocorrelation within
    trajectories, partial dependence as in Friedman (2001)
    <doi:10.1214/aos/1013203451>, cross-validation by speaker and a
    'ggplot2' theme for papers. The data sets of the courses are in the
    'simling' package.
